Both $d\tau$ and $\phi$ are scalars. The simplest linear coupling is therefore $\boxed{
A
=
\int d\tau\,[-m+\phi(x,t)]
}.$ This choice is not unique. One could replace $\phi$ by any function $F(\phi)$. The linear term is enough to display the physical idea.

